1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,170
Welcome to the technical demonstration of MediCart, a modern, production-grade Android pharmacy application developed for the internship assessment at ALGIONS AI LABS PRIVATE LIMITED.

2
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:22,310
MediCart is designed to make discovering, ordering, and managing essential medicines transparent, secure, and effortless for Indian consumers.

3
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:29,060
Let us walk through the complete end-to-end experience running live on a physical Android device.

4
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:40,290
MediCart features a robust phone number and password authentication system. Users can securely sign in with their ten-digit Indian mobile number.

5
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:45,270
The password field includes an interactive visibility toggle.

6
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:59,990
For new users, registration enforces a real-time criteria checklist ensuring passwords contain upper and lower case letters, numbers, and special symbols, verified through a constant-time HMAC OTP.

7
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:09,480
If a password is forgotten, an anti-enumeration recovery flow allows secure reset while instantly invalidating previous sessions.

8
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:17,900
Logging in brings us to the Home screen, styled with Material Design 3 and an elegant Emerald Green palette.

9
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:23,360
At the top, the deliverable postal PIN code displays serviceability.

10
00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:31,940
Customers can browse through healthcare categories including Pain Relief, Cough and Cold, First Aid, and Vitamins.

11
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:45,730
Navigating to the Catalogue, twenty generic pharmaceutical formulations are fetched dynamically from our live cloud database, showing authentic MRP strikethroughs, discounts, and real-time stock indicators.

12
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:56,100
Opening a medicine reveals complete clinical transparency: active ingredients, dosage warnings, manufacturer details, and return policies.

13
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:59,760
Let's add Paracare 650 to the cart.

14
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:11,430
In the shopping cart, MediCart enforces strict Indian e-pharmacy regulatory compliance: users are capped at a maximum of five packs per formulation to prevent hoarding.

15
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:20,700
The transparent fee engine computes item totals, a flat delivery fee of thirty rupees, and hygienic packaging in integer paise.

16
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:27,780
Proceeding to checkout, we confirm our saved delivery address in Indiranagar, Bengaluru.

17
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:40,650
For payment, MediCart offers a simulated non-financial sandbox supporting UPI Demo, Cash on Delivery, and Cards, clearly communicating that no real money is deducted.

18
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:47,810
When placing the order, the client attaches a unique UUID idempotency key in the request header.

19
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:57,590
This guarantees that even during network jitter or accidental double-taps, duplicate orders and double inventory decrements are prevented.

20
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:04,140
The order is confirmed live by the server, generating our unique business reference.

21
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:14,420
Tapping into Order Details displays a four-stage visual timeline: Order Confirmed, Dispensing and Packing, Out for Delivery, and Delivered.

22
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:20,810
The line items preserve an immutable snapshot of prices at the moment of checkout.

23
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:27,920
In Order History, past orders remain fully accessible, synchronized with MongoDB.

24
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:33,750
Behind the scenes, reliability and security are top priorities.

25
00:03:33,999 --> 00:03:46,170
On the client, authentication tokens are stored using Android Jetpack Security's EncryptedSharedPreferences, protected by AES-256 GCM in the hardware Keystore.

26
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:59,500
When network connectivity drops, the repository automatically falls back to an offline SQLite database, ensuring users can still access saved medicines and cart items without interruption.

27
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:13,470
MediCart's modern architecture combines Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, and MVVM on Android with a Node.js, Express, and MongoDB Atlas backend deployed publicly on Render.

28
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:28,190
The system has undergone rigorous automated testing, achieving a one hundred percent pass rate across forty-nine Android unit tests and thirty-nine backend API tests, totaling eighty-eight verified test cases.

29
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:32,460
Thank you for reviewing the MediCart demonstration.

30
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:42,170
With native Android excellence, cloud scalability, and pharmaceutical safety compliance, MediCart is fully prepared for evaluation.

31
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:46,280
Developed with dedication by Sahil Kumar Chaudhary.
